WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.610
Welcome to part 1 of the First Time Homebuyer Series and this series we're going to be going over how to buy your first home.

2
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:12.110
Buying your first home can be very stressful, but with the right preparation and guidance can be one of the most rewarding decisions of your life.

3
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:21.610
In this first episode we're going to be going over the fundamentals, how to choose the right area for you, how to make a budget, how to prepare financially, and lastly how to choose the best realtor for you.

4
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:25.610
When choosing the right area for you, you have to ask yourself what's important to you.

5
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:32.110
Do you care about the quality of the school? Do you need to be close to restaurants, stores, and parks? Do you need to be close to work or an MTA?

6
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:35.110
So it really depends on what's important to you.

7
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.610
When setting your realistic budget, you don't want your mortgage to be more than 33% of your income.

8
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:45.110
For example, if you make $10,000 a month, you don't want your mortgage payments to be more than $3,300 a month.

9
00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:52.610
For getting prepared financially, you want to interview two or three mortgage brokers and have them compete against each other to see who can get you the most favorable rate.

10
00:00:52.610 --> 00:01:01.610
When choosing your realtor, you should sit down with him, interview him, ask him if he knows about any first time home buyer programs and incentives to help you with your down payment or closing costs.

11
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:06.610
You should ask him if they have a trusted lender, attorney, and inspector that they use.

12
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:10.610
Ask them how they plan on negotiating on your behalf to get you the best deal.

13
00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:16.610
And most importantly, just trust your instincts because you're going to be working closely with this realtor for the next 6 months to 12 months.

14
00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:23.610
If you'd like a free home buyer guide, or you see a homeownership on the horizons for you in the next 6 months to 2 years,

15
00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:27.610
DM me directly or call me at 917-951-2142
